{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1706211141","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-wtNLM62CGYARJb7Qhv86A8","dateCreated":"2025-03-14T18:25:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-03-14T18:37:10+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/03/amazon-data-firehose-real-time-streaming-data-s3-tables/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are excited to announce the general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e (Firehose) integration with Amazon S3 Tables, a feature that enables customers to deliver real-time streaming data into Amazon S3 Tables without requiring any code development or multi-step processes.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFirehose can acquire streaming data from Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon MSK, Direct PUT API, and AWS Services such as AWS WAF web ACL logs, Amazon VPC Flow Logs. It can then deliver this data to destinations like Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, Snowflake, and others for analytics. Now, with the Amazon S3 Table integration, customers can stream data from any of these sources directly into Amazon S3 Tables. As a serverless service, Firehose allows customers to simply setup a stream by configuring the source and destination properties, and pay based on bytes processed.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new feature also enables customers to route records in a data stream to different Amazon S3 tables based on the content of the incoming record. Additionally, customers can automate processing for data correction and right-to-forget scenarios by applying row-level update or delete operations in the destination S3 tables.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/apache-iceberg-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2025-03-14T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose now delivers real-time streaming data into Amazon S3 Tables"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1680837876","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-i9qtgCvs5ea3Vtsu2U8prc","dateCreated":"2025-02-24T19:55:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-02-26T18:08:56+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in AWS Asia Pacific (Thailand) and Mexico (Central) regions. Amazon Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data into Amazon S3, Apache Iceberg Tables, Amazon S3 Tables, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and third party analytics applications such as Splunk and Datadog, enabling real-time analytics use cases.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith Amazon Data Firehose, you don\u0026#39;t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. To get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFor Amazon Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/02/amazon-data-firehose-thailand-mexico-central-regions/","postDateTime":"2025-02-26T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose is now available in AWS Asia Pacific (Thailand) and Mexico (Central) regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p162594329","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"whD8r5EnbZnq3jMMjp4tnC","dateCreated":"2024-11-06T21:48:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-15T20:38:56+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose now enables capture and replication of database changes to Apache Iceberg Tables in Amazon S3 (Preview) . This new feature allows customers to easily stream real-time data from MySQL and PostgreSQL databases directly into Apache Iceberg Tables.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFirehose is a fully managed, serverless streaming service that enables customers to capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, Snowflake, and other destinations for analytics. With this functionality, Firehose performs an initial complete data copy from selected database tables, then continuously streams Change Data Capture (CDC) updates to reflect inserts, updates, and deletions in the Apache Iceberg Tables .This streamlined solution eliminates complex data pipeline setups while minimizing impact on database transaction performance .\u003cbr /\u003e\nKey capabilities include: \u0026bull; Automatic creation of Apache Iceberg Tables matching source database schemas \u0026bull; Automatic schema evolution in response to source changes \u0026bull; Selective replication of specific databases, tables, and columns\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis preview feature is available in all AWS regions except China, AWS GovCloud (US), and Asia Pacific (Malaysia) Regions. For terms and conditions, see Beta Service Participation in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-terms/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Terms\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/database-as-source-iceberg.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about this feature, visit this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/replicate-changes-from-databases-to-apache-iceberg-tables-using-amazon-data-firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS blog post\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-data-firehose-continuous-replication-database-changes-apache-iceberg-tables-s3","postDateTime":"2024-11-15T15:30:00-05:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose supports continuous replication of database changes to Apache Iceberg Tables in Amazon S3"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p165692833","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"8R3Pyi6TQnNopD3sMh8vs2","dateCreated":"2024-11-06T20:08:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-06T20:37:52+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose support for delivering data streams into Apache Iceberg tables in Amazon S3 is now available in all AWS regions except AWS China, AWS GovCloud and ap-southeast-5 regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith this feature, Firehose integrates with Apache Iceberg, so customers can deliver data streams directly into Apache Iceberg tables in their Amazon S3 data lake. Firehose can acquire data streams from Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon MSK, or Direct PUT API, and is also integrated to acquire streams from AWS Services such as AWS WAF web ACL logs, Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon VPC Flow Logs, AWS IOT, Amazon SNS, AWS API Gateway Access logs and many others listed \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-name.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. Customers can stream data from any of these sources directly into Apache Iceberg tables in Amazon S3, and avoid multi-step processes. Firehose is serverless, so customers can simply setup a stream by configuring the source and destination properties, and pay based on bytes processed.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new feature also allows customers to route records in a data stream to different Apache Iceberg tables based on the content of the incoming record. To route records to different tables, customers can configure routing rules using JSON expressions. Additionally, customers can specify if the incoming record should apply a row-level update or delete operation in the destination Apache Iceberg table, and automate processing for data correction and right to forget scenarios.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more and get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/apache-iceberg-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-data-firehose-support-data-apache-iceberg-tables-additional-regions","postDateTime":"2024-11-06T16:00:00-05:00","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose support for delivering data into Apache Iceberg tables is available in additional AWS Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p149833665","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-1CyYXLvHR6puRJFk9Kw2ha","dateCreated":"2024-09-30T18:05:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-10-01T17:53:21+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e (Firehose) can now deliver data streams into Apache Iceberg tables in Amazon S3.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFirehose enables customers to acquire, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, Snowflake, and other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, Firehose integrates with Apache Iceberg, so customers can deliver data streams directly into Apache Iceberg tables in their Amazon S3 data lake. Firehose can acquire data streams from Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon MSK, or Direct PUT API, and is also integrated to acquire streams from AWS Services such as AWS WAF web ACL logs, Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon VPC Flow Logs, AWS IOT, Amazon SNS, AWS API Gateway Access logs and many others listed \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-name.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. Customers can stream data from any of these sources directly into Apache Iceberg tables in Amazon S3, and avoid multi-step processes. Firehose is serverless, so customers can simply setup a stream by configuring the source and destination properties, and pay based on bytes processed.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new feature also allows customers to route records in a data stream to different Apache Iceberg tables based on the content of the incoming record. To route records to different tables, customers can configure routing rules using JSON expressions. Additionally, customers can specify if the incoming record should apply a row-level update or delete operation in the destination Apache Iceberg table, and automate processing for data correction and right to forget scenarios.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/apache-iceberg-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/10/amazon-data-firehose-data-streams-iceberg-format-tables-s3/","postDateTime":"2024-10-01T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose delivers data streams into Apache Iceberg format tables in Amazon S3"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#d153510116","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-4eNxHGzeEE6tU7kaDPGQFT","dateCreated":"2024-08-16T18:54:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-08-22T17:02:22+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use Amazon Data Firehose in the AWS Asia Pacific (Malaysia) region. Amazon Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, Snowflake, Apache Iceberg, and third party analytics applications such as Splunk and Datadog, enabling real-time analytics use cases.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith Amazon Data Firehose, you don\u0026#39;t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. To get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFor Amazon Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/08/amazon-data-firehose-asia-pacific-malaysia-region/","postDateTime":"2024-08-22T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Malaysia) region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p131198026","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"5BasFJpphxBV2kfCWhbYuG","dateCreated":"2024-05-30T18:48:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-06-07T17:02:05+0000","additionalFields":{"regionalAvailability":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Firehose supports using AWS Secrets Manager for keys to connect to the following destinations: Amazon Redshift, custom HTTP endpoint, Snowflake, Splunk, Coralogix, Datadog, Dynatrace, Elastic, Honeycomb, LogicMonitor, Logz.io, MongoDB Cloud, and New Relic. The feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/using-secrets-manager.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e (Firehose) now supports integration with AWS Secrets Manager (Secrets Manager) to configure secrets such as database credentials or keys to connect to streaming destinations such as Amazon Redshift, Snowflake, Splunk, and HTTP endpoints.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon Data Firehose needs to access a secret such as database credentials or keys to connect to a streaming destination. With this launch, Amazon Data Firehose can retrieve a secret from Secrets Manager instead of using a plain text secret in configuration to connect to the destination. By using Secrets Manager integration, you can ensure that secrets are not visible in plain text during Firehose stream creation workflow either in AWS Management Console or API parameters. This feature provides a more secure practice to store and maintain a secret in Firehose and allows you to leverage automatic secret rotation capability provided by Secrets Manager.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/06/amazon-data-firehose-integration-secrets-manager","postDateTime":"2024-06-07T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose now supports integration with AWS Secrets Manager"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-04-stream-data-amazon-data-firehose-snowflake-snowpipe-streaming","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/stream-data-amazon-data-firehose-snowflake-snowpipe-streaming/","dateCreated":"2024-04-17T19:26:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:48:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose (Firehose) now offers direct integration with Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming. Firehose enables customers to reliably capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Splunk, and other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can stream clickstream, application, and AWS service logs from multiple sources, including Kinesis Data Streams, to Snowflake. With a few clicks, customers can setup a Firehose stream to deliver data to Snowflake. Firehose automatically scales to stream gigabytes of data, and records are available in Snowflake within seconds.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSnowflake offers two options to load data into Snowflake tables: Snowpipe and Snowpipe Streaming. With Snowpipe, customers load data from files in micro-batches. This requires aggregating streams into batches, writing to interim storage, and then loading into Snowflake. This multi-step process introduces several minutes of latency, and higher cost. Snowpipe Streaming enables writing rows of data into tables. Through integration with Snowpipe Streaming, Firehose delivers streams record-by-record as soon as available, so data is available for querying in Snowflake within seconds. Thus, customers reduce cost, latency, and complexity of delivering streams into Snowflake.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more and get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-04-17T19:26:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/stream-data-amazon-data-firehose-snowflake-snowpipe-streaming/","postDateTime":"2024-04-17T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream data into Snowflake using Amazon Data Firehose and Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose (Firehose) now offers direct integration with Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming. Firehose enables customers to reliably capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Splunk, and other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can stream clickstream, application, and AWS service logs from multiple sources, including Kinesis Data Streams, to Snowflake. With a few clicks, customers can setup a Firehose stream to deliver data to Snowflake. Firehose automatically scales to stream gigabytes of data, and records are available in Snowflake within seconds.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-02-amazon-data-firehose-message-extraction-cloudwatch-logs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-message-extraction-cloudwatch-logs/","dateCreated":"2024-02-27T18:04:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:46:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose (Firehose) decompression for CloudWatch Logs now supports message extraction, so customers can automatically filter out header information and deliver only the message content from their CloudWatch logs to destinations such as Amazon S3 and Splunk for analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers use Firehose to decompress, aggregate, and deliver log events from their applications and services captured in Amazon CloudWatch Logs to destinations such as Amazon S3 and Splunk for use cases such as application troubleshooting and audit compliance. CloudWatch log records use a nested JSON structure, and the message in each record is embedded within header information. Many customers want to filter out the header information and simply deliver the embedded message to the destination, because it reduces the cost of subsequent processing and storage. With message extraction, Firehose provides a simple option that customers can select to filter out the header information and only deliver the embedded message content. There is no additional charge to apply message extraction when customers use Firehose decompression for CloudWatch Logs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about the feature and get started, visit Amazon Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html#Message_extraction\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-27T18:04:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-message-extraction-cloudwatch-logs/","postDateTime":"2024-02-27T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose adds message extraction feature for decompressed CloudWatch Logs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Data Firehose (Firehose) decompression for CloudWatch Logs now supports message extraction, so customers can automatically filter out header information and deliver only the message content from their CloudWatch logs to destinations such as Amazon S3 and Splunk for analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-02-amazon-data-firehose-time-zone-bucket-prefixes","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-time-zone-bucket-prefixes/","dateCreated":"2024-02-16T22:20:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now\u0026nbsp;enables selecting a time zone for bucket prefixes when delivering streams to Amazon S3,\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers use Amazon Data Firehose to deliver data streams to Amazon S3 data lakes, data warehouses, and analytics services. When delivering streams to Amazon S3, Firehose enables adding a UTC time prefix in the format YYYY/MM/dd/HH before writing objects to Amazon S3. The prefix enables creating a logical hierarchy in the Amazon S3 bucket, where each forward slash (/) creates a level in the hierarchy. With this feature, customers can specify a time zone that they want to use for their Amazon S3 bucket prefix.  As a result, customers that want their data in Amazon S3 to use bucket prefixes in a non-UTC time zone format do not have to resort to additional post-processing operations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Firehose is available. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-deliver.html#s3-object-name\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-16T22:08:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-time-zone-bucket-prefixes/","postDateTime":"2024-02-16T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose enables selecting a time zone for bucket prefixes when delivering streams to Amazon S3","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now\u0026nbsp;enables selecting a time zone for bucket prefixes when delivering streams to Amazon S3,\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-02-amazon-data-firehose-formerly-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-formerly-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2024-02-09T22:46:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS is renaming Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to Amazon Data Firehose. Amazon Data Firehose is the easiest way to capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Splunk, Snowflake, and other 3rd party analytics services. The name change is effective in the AWS Management Console, documentation, and service web pages. There are no other changes, including service endpoints, APIs, the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) access policies, and Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Your existing applications will continue to work as they did previously.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Data Firehose, you can reduce the complexity of maintaining streaming data delivery pipelines. Amazon Data Firehose will manage the provisioning and scaling of resources on your behalf. Amazon Data Firehose integrates with Amazon Kinesis Data Streams (KDS), Amazon Managed Streaming for Kafka (MSK), and over 20 other AWS sources to ingest streaming data. You can also ingest data directly from your own data sources using the Direct PUT API. You can transform your data streams into formats like Parquet and ORC, and dynamically partition data to write to the Amazon S3 destination bucket with different S3 prefixes using metadata attributes. You pay for the amount of data you process through the service with no minimum fee or setup cost.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about the AWS Regions where Amazon Data Firehose is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region\u003c/a\u003e table. To learn more, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T21:32:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-formerly-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2024-02-09T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Data Firehose, formerly known as Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS is renaming Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to Amazon Data Firehose. Amazon Data Firehose is the easiest way to capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Splunk, Snowflake, and other 3rd party analytics services. The name change is effective in the AWS Management Console, documentation, and service web pages. There are no other changes, including service endpoints, APIs, the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) access policies, and Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Your existing applications will continue to work as they did previously.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-01-stream-data-snowflake-kinesis-data-firehose-snowpipe-streaming-preview","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/stream-data-snowflake-kinesis-data-firehose-snowpipe-streaming-preview/","dateCreated":"2024-02-02T13:39:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:59:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose (Firehose) now offers direct integration with Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming in preview. Firehose enables customers to reliably capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Splunk, and other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can stream clickstream, application, and AWS service logs from multiple sources, including Kinesis Data Streams, to Snowflake. With a few clicks, customers can setup a Firehose stream to deliver data to Snowflake. Firehose automatically scales to stream gigabytes of data, and records are available in Snowflake within seconds.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSnowflake offers two options to load data into Snowflake tables: Snowpipe and Snowpipe Streaming. With Snowpipe, customers load data from files in micro-batches. This requires aggregating streams into batches, writing to interim storage, and then loading into Snowflake. This multi-step process introduces several minutes of latency, and higher cost. Snowpipe Streaming enables writing rows of data into tables. Through integration with Snowpipe Streaming, Firehose delivers streams record-by-record as soon as available, so data is available for querying in Snowflake within seconds. Thus, customers reduce cost, latency, and complexity of delivering streams into Snowflake.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFirehose integration with Snowflake is available in preview in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), and Europe (Ireland) AWS Regions. To learn more and get started, visit Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e,  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e. Preview features are provided for evaluation and testing, and should not be used in production systems. For terms and conditions, see Beta Service Participation in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-terms/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Terms\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-01-19T22:18:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/stream-data-snowflake-kinesis-data-firehose-snowpipe-streaming-preview/","postDateTime":"2024-01-19T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream data into Snowflake using Kinesis Data Firehose and Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming (Preview)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose (Firehose) now offers direct integration with Snowflake Snowpipe Streaming in preview. Firehose enables customers to reliably capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Splunk, and other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can stream clickstream, application, and AWS service logs from multiple sources, including Kinesis Data Streams, to Snowflake. With a few clicks, customers can setup a Firehose stream to deliver data to Snowflake. Firehose automatically scales to stream gigabytes of data, and records are available in Snowflake within seconds.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-02-amazon-data-firehose-specifying-file-extension-data-streams-s3","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-specifying-file-extension-data-streams-s3/","dateCreated":"2024-02-16T22:09:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:55:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports specifying a file extension for objects delivered to S3 destinations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers use Amazon Data Firehose to deliver data streams to Amazon S3 data lakes, data warehouses, and analytics services. With this feature, customers can specify a file extension when their Firehose data stream is written to Amazon S3 objects. For example, when delivering data streams in compressed GZIP format, customers can set up their Firehose stream to append a .gzip file extension to objects created in Amazon S3, so that applications that use AWS analytics services such as Amazon Athena and Amazon EMR to process their data in Amazon S3 can automatically infer the data format based on the file extension.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-deliver.html#s3-object-name\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-16T22:08:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-data-firehose-specifying-file-extension-data-streams-s3/","postDateTime":"2024-01-16T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Data Firehose now supports specifying a file extension for data streams delivered to Amazon S3","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports specifying a file extension for objects delivered to S3 destinations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-splunk-alb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-splunk-alb/","dateCreated":"2024-02-02T13:44:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:04:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose (Firehose) enables customers to capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, and 10+ other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can now use Firehose to deliver streams to their Splunk cluster configured with either an Application Load Balancer (ALB) or a Classic Load Balancer (CLB).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFirehose support of ALB is available at no additional cost. To learn more about the feature and get started, visit Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html#create-destination-splunk\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-01-10T20:20:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-splunk-alb/","postDateTime":"2024-01-10T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Data Firehose supports delivering data to Splunk clusters using ALB","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose (Firehose) enables customers to capture, transform, and deliver data streams into Amazon S3, Redshift, OpenSearch, Splunk, and 10+ other destinations for analytics. With this new feature, customers can now use Firehose to deliver streams to their Splunk cluster configured with either an Application Load Balancer (ALB) or a Classic Load Balancer (CLB).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-canada-calgary-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-canada-calgary-region/","dateCreated":"2023-12-20T18:41:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and third party analytics applications such as Splunk and Datadog, enabling real-time analytics use cases.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. To get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-12-20T18:41:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-canada-calgary-region/","postDateTime":"2023-12-20T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and third party analytics applications such as Splunk and Datadog, enabling real-time analytics use cases.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations/","dateCreated":"2023-12-15T17:59:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers decompressed CloudWatch Logs to S3 and Splunk destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Logs enable customers to aggregate log events from their systems, applications, and services for monitoring purposes. Customers use Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscriptions to deliver log events using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to Amazon S3 and Splunk for troubleshooting and monitoring use cases. CloudWatch Logs are delivered as gzip-compressed objects and with the support of decompression for Cloudwatch Logs in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, customers can now automatically deliver decompressed logs. This eliminates the need for additional services or post-processing to do decompression and allows customers to use optional Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose features such as Data Format Conversion or Dynamic Partitioning.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data. To get started with Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:46:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations/","postDateTime":"2023-12-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose supports delivery of decompressed CloudWatch Logs to destinations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers decompressed CloudWatch Logs to S3 and Splunk destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-09-amazon-msk-data-s3-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/09/amazon-msk-data-s3-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:03:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now integrates with Amazon MSK to offer a fully managed solution that simplifies the processing and delivery of streaming data from Amazon MSK Apache Kafka clusters into data lakes stored on Amazon S3. With just a few clicks, Amazon MSK customers can continuously load data from their desired Apache Kafka clusters to their Amazon S3 bucket, eliminating the need to develop or run their own connector applications.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon MSK is a fully managed service for Apache Kafka that makes it easier for you to build and run applications that use Apache Kafka as a data store. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that continuously captures, transforms, and delivers streaming data to data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. Kinesis Data Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your Amazon MSK data and without ongoing administration. Kinesis Data Firehose also offers easy to use features like JSON to Parquet/ORC for format conversion and batch aggregation to optimize the S3 file size. These features simplify data analytical/processing workflows on delivered data.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon MSK to Amazon S3 delivery using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose can be used in all commercial and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewhere Amazon MSK and Kinesis Data Firehose are available\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:46:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/09/amazon-msk-data-s3-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2023-09-27T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon MSK now supports fully managed data delivery to Amazon S3 using Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now integrates with Amazon MSK to offer a fully managed solution that simplifies the processing and delivery of streaming data from Amazon MSK Apache Kafka clusters into data lakes stored on Amazon S3. With just a few clicks, Amazon MSK customers can continuously load data from their desired Apache Kafka clusters to their Amazon S3 bucket, eliminating the need to develop or run their own connector applications.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-msk","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-msk","description":"general:products/amazon-msk","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third-party providers like Splunk and Datadog etc., enabling near real-time analytics. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write any code to process and deliver your data. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\nFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003csub\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:42:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2023-08-01T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:00:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:48:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/redshift-serverless/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can more easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into Amazon Redshift Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless allows you to run and scale analytics without having to provision and manage data warehouse clusters. With Amazon Redshift Serverless, all users including data analysts, developers, and data scientists, can use Amazon Redshift to get insights from data in seconds. You only pay for the compute used for the duration of the workloads on a per-second basis. You can benefit from this simplicity without making any changes to your existing analytics and business intelligence applications. You can configure the Amazon Redshift Serverless instance to be publicly accessible and start using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose with it to reliably load real-time streams.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose with Amazon Redshift Serverless is generally available in the regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/redshift-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e under Redshift Serverless API section.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:40:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless/","postDateTime":"2023-06-19T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for data stream delivery to Amazon Redshift Serverless","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/redshift/redshift-serverless.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can more easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into Amazon Redshift Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e customers can now send data to Amazon OpenSearch Service using OpenSearch Service auto-generated document ID option. This configuration option enables write-heavy operations, such as log analytics and observability, to consume fewer CPU resources at the OpenSearch domain, resulting in improved performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into Amazon OpenSearch Service and Amazon OpenSearch Serverless. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:34:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service/","postDateTime":"2023-05-11T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for document ID that is auto-generated by Amazon OpenSearch Service","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e customers can now send data to Amazon OpenSearch Service using OpenSearch Service auto-generated document ID option. This configuration option enables write-heavy operations, such as log analytics and observability, to consume fewer CPU resources at the OpenSearch domain, resulting in improved performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third-party providers like Splunk and Datadog etc., enabling near real-time analytics. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:32:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2023-03-13T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-delivery-elastic","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-delivery-elastic/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:02:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Elastic. With this integration, Elastic users have an easier way to ingest streaming data to Elastic and consume the Elastic Stack (ELK Stack) solutions for enterprise search, observability, and security without having to manage applications or write code.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Splunk and Datadog. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all of the underlying stream management with no ongoing administration required. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write delivery applications or manage resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eElastic is an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://partners.amazonaws.com/partners/001E000001A1vNOIAZ/Elastic\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS ISV Partner\u003c/a\u003e that helps you find information, gain insights, and protect your data when you run on Amazon Web Services (AWS). Elastic offers enterprise search, observability, and security that are built on a single, flexible technology stack that can be deployed anywhere.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e and specify Elastic as the destination. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003csub\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:28:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-delivery-elastic/","postDateTime":"2023-03-08T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to Elastic","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Elastic. With this integration, Elastic users have an easier way to ingest streaming data to Elastic and consume the Elastic Stack (ELK Stack) solutions for enterprise search, observability, and security without having to manage applications or write code.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-europe-zurich-spain-hyderabad-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-europe-zurich-spain-hyderabad-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:39:04+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Europe (Zurich), Europe (Spain), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog etc. enabling near real-time analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e. For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csup\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:25:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-europe-zurich-spain-hyderabad-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-02-02T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in Europe (Zurich), Europe (Spain), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) AWS regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Europe (Zurich), Europe (Spain), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-logz-io","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-logz-io/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Logz.io, enabling Logz.io users to ingest streaming metrics and logs without having to manage applications or write code.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Logz.io. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write delivery applications or manage resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability makes it easier than ever to route your AWS Service metrics and logs data directly into Logz.io. The Logz.io Cloud Observability Platform delivers the ELK Stack and Grafana as a fully-managed service so engineers can use the open source monitoring tools they know on a single solution, without the hassle of maintaining them at scale. On top of the managed open source, Logz.io provides additional advanced analytics capabilities to make the ELK Stack and Grafana faster, more integrated, and easier to use.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify Logz as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to Logz.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-08T21:26:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-logz-io/","postDateTime":"2022-12-08T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers to Logz.io ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Logz.io, enabling Logz.io users to ingest streaming metrics and logs without having to manage applications or write code.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-support-data-stream-delivery-opensearch-serverless","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-support-data-stream-delivery-opensearch-serverless/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/features/serverless/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon OpenSearch Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into an Amazon OpenSearch Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOpenSearch Serverless is a new serverless option offered by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon OpenSearch Service\u003c/a\u003e. OpenSearch Serverless makes it simple to run petabyte scale search and analytics workloads without having to configure, manage, or scale OpenSearch clusters. OpenSearch Serverless automatically provisions and scales the underlying resources to deliver fast data ingestion and query responses for even the most demanding and unpredictable workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-30T01:11:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-support-data-stream-delivery-opensearch-serverless/","postDateTime":"2022-11-29T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for data stream delivery to Amazon OpenSearch Serverless","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/opensearch-service/features/serverless.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon OpenSearch Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into an Amazon OpenSearch Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-opensearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-opensearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-opensearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:26:10+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:38:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog, enabling near real-time analytics.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-04T21:11:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2022-11-04T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the Middle East (UAE) AWS region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog, enabling near real-time analytics.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:46:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now deliver Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs directly to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, allowing you to stream your flow logs real-time to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edestinations supported by Amazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edownstream logging solutions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;via custom HTTP endpoints.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Logs enable you to capture and log information about your VPC network traffic. Until today, you could deliver VPC Flow Logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3). With this release, you can now stream your flow logs in real-time to supported Amazon Kinesis Firehose destinations. In addition, you can also use AWS Lambda functions on Amazon Kinesis to enrich or transform the VPC Flow logs while delivering them to downstream logging solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Log delivery to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available through the AWS Management Console, the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), and the AWS Software Development Kit (AWS SDK). To get started, simply create a new flow log subscription and select Amazon Kinesis Firehose as a destination. To learn more about Amazon VPC Flow Logs delivery to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, please refer to the Amazon Kinesis Firehose documentation and VPC Flow Logs documentation. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e to learn about AWS Partner Network solutions that support ingestion of VPC Flow Logs to Amazon Kinesis Firehose. Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloudWatch pricing\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for cost of delivering VPC Flow Logs to Amazon Kinesis Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Logs delivery to Amazon Kinesis Firehose is generally available in the following AWS Regions:\u0026nbsp;US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Northern California), US West (Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Osaka), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (London), Europe (Milan), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Middle East (Bahrain), AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-08T21:23:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","postDateTime":"2022-09-08T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs can now be delivered to Amazon Kinesis Firehose ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now deliver Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs directly to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, allowing you to stream your flow logs real-time to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edestinations supported by Amazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edownstream logging solutions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;via custom HTTP endpoints.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-04-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-coralogix","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-coralogix/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:19:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports streaming data delivery to Coralogix, enabling Coralogix users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Coralogix. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability makes it easier than ever to route your AWS log data directly into Coralogix. With these logs available in Coralogix, you can explore and analyze logs to gain deeper insights into the state of your applications and AWS infrastructure. You can analyze all your AWS service logs while storing only the ones you need, and generate metrics from aggregated logs to uncover and alert on trends in your AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify Coralogix as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to Coralogix. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-04-15T20:08:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-coralogix/","postDateTime":"2022-04-15T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers to Coralogix","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports streaming data delivery to Coralogix, enabling Coralogix users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:16:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://partners.amazonaws.com/partners/0010L00001rElnvQAC/Honeycomb\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHoneycomb\u003c/a\u003e, enabling Honeycomb users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Honeycomb. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability makes it easier than ever to route your AWS log data directly into Honeycomb. With these logs available in Honeycomb, you can instrument your own code then query, trace, graph, and alert on everything from system-wide events down to individual request traces in real time. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify Honeycomb as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to Honeycomb. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-28T17:51:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb/","postDateTime":"2022-01-28T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers to Honeycomb","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://partners.amazonaws.com/partners/0010L00001rElnvQAC/Honeycomb\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHoneycomb\u003c/a\u003e, enabling Honeycomb users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-08-introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we announced Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. With Dynamic Partitioning, you can continuously partition streaming data in Kinesis Data Firehose using keys within data like “customer_id” or “transaction_id” and deliver data grouped by these keys into corresponding Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) prefixes, making it easier for you to run high performance, cost-efficient analytics on streaming data in Amazon S3 using Amazon Athena, Amazon EMR, and Amazon Redshift Spectrum.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePartitioning your data minimizes the amount of data scanned, optimizing performance and reducing costs of your analytics queries on Amazon S3, and increasing granular access to data. Traditionally, customers use Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams to capture and load their data streams into Amazon S3. To partition a streaming data set for Amazon S3-based analytics, customers would need to run partitioning applications between Amazon S3 buckets prior to making the data available for analysis, which could become complicated or costly.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eNow with Dynamic Partitioning, Kinesis Data Firehose will continuously group data in-transit by dynamically or statically defined data keys, and deliver to individual Amazon S3 prefixes by key. This will reduce time-to-insight by minutes or hours, reducing costs and simplifying architectures. Along with Apache Parquet and Apache ORC format conversion features, this feature makes Kinesis Data Firehose the best place to capture, prepare, and load analytics-ready streaming data to Amazon S3.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/dynamic-partitioning.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e to get started with dynamic partitioning, or visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about on-demand pricing for dynamic partitioning. Dynamic partitioning can be used in all commercial AWS regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewhere Kinesis Data Firehose is available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-08T19:48:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2021-08-31T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we announced Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. With Dynamic Partitioning, you can continuously partition streaming data in Kinesis Data Firehose using keys within data like “customer_id” or “transaction_id” and deliver data grouped by these keys into corresponding Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) prefixes, making it easier for you to run high performance, cost-efficient analytics on streaming data in Amazon S3 using Amazon Athena, Amazon EMR, and Amazon Redshift Spectrum.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-athena","description":"general:products/amazon-athena","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#emr-studio","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"emr-studio","description":"general:products/emr-studio","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:30:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-08-aws-data-streaming-solution-amazon-msk-support-aws-iam-streamline-access-control-management","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/aws-data-streaming-solution-amazon-msk-support-aws-iam-streamline-access-control-management/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis release adds support for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/security-iam.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eIAM access control\u003c/a\u003e when creating the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/msk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e cluster. By using IAM Access Control, customers no longer need to build and run one-off access management systems to control client authentication and authorization for Apache Kafka.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAlso included is support for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/msk/latest/developerguide/msk-password.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSASL/SCRAM authentication\u003c/a\u003e when creating the Amazon MSK cluster or when configuring an AWS Lambda function to read data from Amazon MSK. As such, username and password credentials are stored in AWS Secrets Manager. This implementation reduces the overhead of maintaining a traditional Apache Kafka authentication system, including: auditing, updating, and rotating client credentials.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional AWS Solutions are available on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementation\u003c/a\u003e webpage, where customers can browse solutions by product category or industry to find AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-08-04T15:26:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/aws-data-streaming-solution-amazon-msk-support-aws-iam-streamline-access-control-management/","postDateTime":"2021-08-04T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Data Streaming Solution for Amazon MSK adds support for AWS IAM to streamline access control management","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-aws-data-streaming-solution-for-amazon-msk-adds-support-for-apache-kafka-versions-2-8-0-and-2-6-2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-data-streaming-solution-for-amazon-msk-adds-support-for-apache-kafka-versions-2-8-0-and-2-6-2/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis release adds support for Apache Kafka \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-msk-adds-support-apache-kafka-version-2-8-0/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eversion 2.8.0\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-msk-adds-support-for-apache-kafka-version-2-6-2/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eversion 2.6.2\u003c/a\u003e which includes security fixes and features that improve performance. This update also adds a new parameter allowing customers to save on cost by providing the size (in GiB) of the EBS volume for the broker nodes and provides support for enhanced partition-level monitoring to the Amazon MSK cluster (when enabled, this monitoring level makes consumer lag metrics available in Amazon CloudWatch).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAlso included in this update are AWS CDK assets that have been developed for use with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://amazonmsk-labs.workshop.aws/en/overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon MSK Labs\u003c/a\u003e, which are a learning resource for getting started with Amazon MSK, and also explains how to leverage advanced features (such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://amazonmsk-labs.workshop.aws/en/cruisecontrol/overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCruise Control\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://amazonmsk-labs.workshop.aws/en/securityencryption/tlsmauth.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTLS mutual authentication\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://amazonmsk-labs.workshop.aws/en/openmonitoring/overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eopen monitoring\u003c/a\u003e). You can apply these features to clusters created using the solution.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional AWS Solutions are available on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementation\u003c/a\u003e webpage, where customers can browse solutions by product category or industry to find AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-19T16:22:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-data-streaming-solution-for-amazon-msk-adds-support-for-apache-kafka-versions-2-8-0-and-2-6-2/","postDateTime":"2021-05-19T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Solutions Implementation - AWS Data Streaming Solution for Amazon MSK adds support for Apache Kafka versions 2.8.0 and 2.6.2","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-solution","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-solution","description":"general:products/aws-solution","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-02-aws-solutions-implementation-aws-data-streaming-solution","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/02/aws-solutions-implementation-aws-data-streaming-solution/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:01:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"The AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data. This update adds a template that accelerates development of streaming data workloads by reducing the need for you to model and provision resources using AWS CloudFormation; set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms, dashboards, and logging; and manually implement streaming data best practices in AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe newly introduced template deploys a reference architecture that streams data from an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/msk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e cluster. The streaming data events are subsequently read by an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e application and the output is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. Also, it showcases the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://ci.apache.org/projects/flink/flink-docs-stable/dev/table/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eApache Flink Table API\u003c/a\u003e, which allows you to interact with data in a stream using a relational model and exactly-once guarantees.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional AWS Solutions are available on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementation\u003c/a\u003e webpage, where you can browse solutions by product category or industry to find AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-02-05T20:45:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/02/aws-solutions-implementation-aws-data-streaming-solution/","postDateTime":"2021-02-05T18:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Solutions Implementation - AWS Data Streaming Solution for Amazon MSK adds a template for you to read events and store data to Amazon S3 from a streaming application","postSummary":"The AWS Solutions team recently updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-msk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data. This update adds a template that accelerates development of streaming data workloads by reducing the need for you to model and provision resources using AWS CloudFormation; set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms, dashboards, and logging; and manually implement streaming data best practices in AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-01-amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)\u003c/a\u003e to deliver messages to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. This new subscription type for SNS enables message storage, analytics, and auditing by providing a simple way to send Amazon SNS messages to data lakes, data stores, and analytics services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis integration makes it easier for customers using Amazon SNS to collect data for analytics and to keep records for backup or audit in applications such as e-commerce and banking. You can use Amazon SNS topics with Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions to capture, transform, buffer, compress and upload data to Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES), HTTP endpoints, and third party service providers such as Datadog, New Relic, MongoDB, and Splunk. With this feature, you can deliver Amazon SNS messages to these destinations without writing custom code.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt launch, Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions for Amazon SNS are available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/sns.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e22 AWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. You can subscribe a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to an Amazon SNS standard topic by using the AWS Software Development Kit (SDK), AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), AWS Management Console, or AWS CloudFormation.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about delivering Amazon SNS messages to Kinesis Data Firehose, see the following:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/introducing-message-archiving-and-analytics-for-amazon-sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eIntroducing message archiving and analytics for Amazon SNS blog post\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-firehose-as-subscriber.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS developer guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/sns/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS console\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-03T18:07:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions/","postDateTime":"2021-01-12T11:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon SNS adds support for message archiving and analytics via Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sns.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)\u003c/a\u003e to deliver messages to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. This new subscription type for SNS enables message storage, analytics, and auditing by providing a simple way to send Amazon SNS messages to data lakes, data stores, and analytics services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-sns","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-sns","description":"general:products/amazon-sns","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud\"\u003eMongoDB Cloud\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to MongoDB Cloud without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like MongoDB. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMongoDB Cloud is a great way to build data-driven applications. The core of MongoDB Cloud is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/aws-mongodb\"\u003eMongoDB Atlas\u003c/a\u003e, an elastic cloud database with built-in Search and Data Lake services for powering diverse workloads through a common API. The streaming delivery from Kinesis Data Firehose to MongoDB is powered by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.mongodb.com/realm/services/configure/service-webhooks/\"\u003eMongoDB Realm webhooks\u003c/a\u003e making it easier than ever to build robust, reactive data pipelines that stream directly into MongoDB collections, and enable real-time querying, enrichment, and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify MongoDB Cloud as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to MongoDB. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, read, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://developer.mongodb.com/how-to/Realm-AWS-Kinesis-Firehose-Destination\"\u003eUsing MongoDB Realm WebHooks with AWS Kinesis Data Firehose Delivery Streams\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on MongoDB, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/\"\u003eMongoDB\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T22:23:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T15:20:54Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to MongoDB Cloud","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud\"\u003eMongoDB Cloud\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to MongoDB Cloud without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-http-endpoints","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-http-endpoints/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to a generic HTTP endpoint. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to an HTTP endpoint without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Datadog, New Relic, MongoDB, and Splunk. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify where to deliver the data. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to the specified AWS service or HTTP endpoint. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/big-data/stream-data-to-an-http-endpoint-with-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eStream data to an HTTP endpoint with Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T22:14:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-http-endpoints/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T12:52:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to HTTP endpoints","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to a generic HTTP endpoint. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to an HTTP endpoint without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-datadog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-datadog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.datadoghq.com/\"\u003eDatadog\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to Datadog without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Datadog. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability makes it easier than ever to route your AWS log data directly into Datadog. With these logs available in Datadog, you can use them with Datadog Log Management and Datadog Security Monitoring to analyze the health, performance, and security of your cloud resources. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify Datadog as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to Datadog. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on Datadog, click \u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.datadoghq.com/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T22:32:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-datadog/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to Datadog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.datadoghq.com/\"\u003eDatadog\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to Datadog without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-new-relic","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-new-relic/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:06:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://newrelic.com/\"\u003eNew Relic\u003c/a\u003e, the industry\u0027s leading observability platform for all telemetry data. This Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to New Relic without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like New Relic. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability makes it easier than ever to get data into New Relic with just a few simple steps. Custom applications and select AWS services can be configured to write logs directly to An Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose that delivers the data stream to platforms like New Relic without additional Amazon CloudWatch cost. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify New Relic as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your observability telemetry data to New Relic. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/big-data/new-relic-drinks-straight-from-the-firehose-consuming-amazon-kinesis-data/\"\u003eNew Relic drinks straight from the Firehose: consuming AWS Kinesis data\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on New Relic, click \u003ca href\u003d\"https://newrelic.com/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T22:30:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-data-delivery-to-new-relic/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to New Relic","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://newrelic.com/\"\u003eNew Relic\u003c/a\u003e, the industry\u0027s leading observability platform for all telemetry data. This Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to New Relic without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-21T15:46:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town/","postDateTime":"2020-07-21T12:25:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/elasticsearch-service/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e domain in an Amazon VPC. You can now easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data in to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain running in a VPC without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you are already using today. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. It can also batch, compress, convert, and encrypt the data before loading it, minimizing the amount of storage used at the destination and increasing security.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service makes it easy for you to deploy, secure, and run Elasticsearch cost effectively at scale. You can build, monitor, and troubleshoot your applications using the tools you love, at the scale you need. The service provides support for open source Elasticsearch APIs, managed Kibana, integration with Logstash and other AWS services, and built-in alerting and SQL querying. With Amazon Elasticsearch Service, you get the ELK stack you need, without the operational overhead.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlacing an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain within a VPC enables secure communication between Amazon Elasticsearch Service and other services within the VPC without the need for an internet gateway, NAT device, or VPN connection. Because of their logical isolation, domains that reside within a VPC have an extra layer of security when compared to domains that use public endpoints.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and Amazon Elasticsearch Service availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-24T21:49:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc/","postDateTime":"2020-04-24T11:41:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for streaming data delivery to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain in an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/elasticsearch-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e domain in an Amazon VPC. You can now easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data in to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain running in a VPC without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose through AWS PrivateLink in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink allows you to privately access services hosted on AWS in a highly available and scalable manner, without using public IPs and without requiring the traffic to traverse the internet. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs are now available to use inside your VPC through AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecommercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e, China Regions, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about this feature, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-11T20:08:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-03-11T12:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose through AWS PrivateLink in the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink allows you to privately access services hosted on AWS in a highly available and scalable manner, without using public IPs and without requiring the traffic to traverse the internet. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs are now available to use inside your VPC through AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now provides additional protection of sensitive data through customer-provided keys for server-side encryption (SSE) of delivery streams. This feature is integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kms/\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service\u003c/a\u003e (KMS), which allows you to centrally manage keys that protect Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams along with keys that protect your other AWS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen you ingest records to encrypted delivery streams, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose immediately encrypts your messages. The encryption takes place on the server, using a 256-bit AES-GCM algorithm and a customer master key (CMK) issued by AWS KMS. Kinesis Data Firehose now works with both customer-provided CMKs and AWS-provided CMKs. The records are stored in encrypted form in multiple availability zones (AZs), and decrypted only as they are delivered to destinations like \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/elasticsearch-service/\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/\"\u003eAmazon Redshift\u003c/a\u003e and Splunk. To learn more, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/security.html\"\u003eSecurity in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability is now available in all AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eavailable\u003c/a\u003e. There are no additional Kinesis Data Firehose charges for using this capability. You are only charged for AWS KMS usage. For pricing details, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kms/pricing/\"\u003eAWS KMS pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-26T21:29:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption/","postDateTime":"2019-11-26T13:09:25Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Adds Support For Customer-Provided Keys for Server-Side Encryption","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now provides additional protection of sensitive data through customer-provided keys for server-side encryption (SSE) of delivery streams. This feature is integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kms.html\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service\u003c/a\u003e (KMS), which allows you to centrally manage keys that protect Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams along with keys that protect your other AWS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-07T19:04:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2019-11-07T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:49:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now configure Amazon API Gateway to send API access logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.  It\u0027s easy to configure Kinesis Data Firehose as a log destination by enabling access logging on an API and specifying the Firehose stream.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChoosing Kinesis Data Firehose as a destination for access logs allows customers to analyze API access patterns in real time and quickly troubleshoot issues using Amazon services like Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, or using 3rd-party tools like Splunk.  For example, using Kinesis Data Firehose integration with S3 allows customers to create Amazon Quicksight dashboards to visualize live API log data.  Customers can also use Splunk\u0027s integration with Kinesis Data Firehose to continuously monitor, diagnose, and resolve issues.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAPI Gateway’s support for Kinesis Data Firehose access logging is generally available in all regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html#fh_region\"\u003eKinesis Data Firehose is available\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, refer to the API Gateway \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-logging-to-kinesis.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-16T17:50:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-10-16T12:07:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon API Gateway now supports access logging to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now configure Amazon API Gateway to send API access logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.  It\u0027s easy to configure Kinesis Data Firehose as a log destination by enabling access logging on an API and specifying the Firehose stream.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:26:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service version 7.x clusters for near real-time data analysis and visualization. Kinesis Data Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all of the underlying stream management.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-09T22:46:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","postDateTime":"2019-10-09T09:57:01Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for data stream delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service 7.x clusters","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service version 7.x clusters for near real-time data analysis and visualization. Kinesis Data Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all of the underlying stream management.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:29:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service across accounts. Now your delivery stream and your Elasticsearch clusters can reside in different accounts. This makes it easier for Amazon Elasticsearch Service customers with multiple accounts to ingest streaming data and analyze it in near real time.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-08T20:49:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","postDateTime":"2019-10-08T14:42:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds cross-account delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service across accounts. Now your delivery stream and your Elasticsearch clusters can reside in different accounts. This makes it easier for Amazon Elasticsearch Service customers with multiple accounts to ingest streaming data and analyze it in near real time.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#applications","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"applications","description":"marketing:marchitecture/applications","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#application-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"application-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/application-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-08-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-in-asia-pacific-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-in-asia-pacific-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-in-asia-pacific-region/","postDateTime":"2019-08-15T09:15:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East)  Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region/","postDateTime":"2019-06-27T08:20:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East)  Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-europe-stockholm-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_the_aws_europe_stockholm_region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_the_aws_europe_stockholm_region/","postDateTime":"2019-05-15T14:11:22Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) region ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-04-expanding-aws-privatelink-support-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to securely ingest data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, securely over the Amazon network. When \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e is used with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, all traffic to a Kinesis Data Firehose from a VPC flows over a private connection. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information go to the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;page or read the techncial\u0026nbsp; documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/vpc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-04-16T04:51:21Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Expanding AWS PrivateLink support for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to securely ingest data.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-03-tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eTag-on create is now available for Kinesis Data Firehose. Upon creation, you can tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the AWS Management Console or using the AWS APIs. By tagging resources at the time of creation you can eliminate the need to run custom tagging scripts after resource creation. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you can now set IAM policies on your Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose during creation using tags. This enables automated policy application to give you more granular control over who has access to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs. You can also enforce the use of tagging and can control which tag keys and values are set on your resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the AWS User Documentation\u0026nbsp;to learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/firehose-tagging.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etag-on create\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/controlling-access.html#tag-based-access-control\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etag-based IAM application\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese capabilities are available at no additional cost in all AWS commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-03-11T11:11:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Tag-on Create and Tag-Based IAM Application for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eTag-on create is now available for Kinesis Data Firehose. Upon creation, you can tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the AWS Management Console or using the AWS APIs. By tagging resources at the time of creation you can eliminate the need to run custom tagging scripts after resource creation. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:19+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e today announced support for custom Amazon S3 prefixes allowing customers more flexibility when configuring S3 paths for data delivery.\u0026nbsp;This new capability enables customers to simplify and accelerate ETL (Extract Transform Load) workflows and to enable data partitions for faster query performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow customers can customize the Amazon S3 prefix using the Apache Hive format and timestamp formats (supported by the Java DateTimeFormatter class). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes/","postDateTime":"2019-02-12T12:14:22Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Announces Support for Custom Amazon S3 Prefixes","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e today announced support for custom Amazon S3 prefixes allowing customers more flexibility when configuring S3 paths for data delivery.\u0026nbsp;This new capability enables customers to simplify and accelerate ETL (Extract Transform Load) workflows and to enable data partitions for faster query performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:18:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an isolated AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","postDateTime":"2019-01-16T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an isolated AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Elasticsearch Service, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To get started, you would need an AWS (China) account. You can request an AWS (China) account by completing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.amazonaws.cn/en/sign-up/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis form\u003c/a\u003e. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.amazonaws.cn/kinesis/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.amazonaws.cn/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-01-16T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, Operated by Sinnet, and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, Operated by NWCD","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Elasticsearch Service, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:18:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available. For more information on availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:23:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:59:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the Resource Groups Tagging API to centrally manage tags and search resources for 6 additional AWS Services: Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, AWS Secrets Manager, AWS Certificate Manager Private CA, AWS IoT Analytics, Amazon Aurora, and AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Resource Groups Tagging API is a single central point reaching across 47 AWS services to programmatically perform operations including tag resources, untag resources, list unique tag keys, list tag values, and search for resources with specific tags. To get started with and to view the list of supported AWS Services, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eResource Groups Tagging API documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services/","postDateTime":"2018-10-11T11:08:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Resource Groups Tagging API Supports Additional AWS Services","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the Resource Groups Tagging API to centrally manage tags and search resources for 6 additional AWS Services: Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, AWS Secrets Manager, AWS Certificate Manager Private CA, AWS IoT Analytics, Amazon Aurora, and AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-secrets-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-secrets-manager","description":"general:products/aws-secrets-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-certificate-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-certificate-manager","description":"general:products/aws-certificate-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-tools-aws-resource-groups","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-tools-aws-resource-groups","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-tools/aws-resource-groups","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:01:31+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-aurora","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-aurora","description":"general:products/amazon-aurora","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iot-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iot-analytics","description":"general:products/aws-iot-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-four-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_four_additional_aws_regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:02:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in EU (London), EU (Paris), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), and South America (Sao Paulo). With the addition of these four regions, Kinesis Data Firehose is available in 15 regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), Canada (Central), South America (Sao Paulo), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), EU (Paris), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Asia Pacific (Mumbai).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://signin.aws.amazon.com/signin?redirect_uri\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fconsole.aws.amazon.com%2Ffirehose%2Fhome%3Fstate%3DhashArgs%2523%252Fwizard%252FnameAndSource%26isauthcode%3Dtrue\u0026amp;client_id\u003darn%3Aaws%3Aiam%3A%3A015428540659%3Auser%2Ffirehose\u0026amp;forceMobileApp\u003d0\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_four_additional_aws_regions/","postDateTime":"2018-06-27T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in Four Additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-in-canada-central-and-asia-pacific-seoul","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Data_Firehose_now_Available_in_Canada_Central_and_Asia_Pacific_Seoul/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:46:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. We are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Data Firehose in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of these two regions, Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in eleven regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Canada (Central).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Firehose can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\"\u003eKinesis management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Data_Firehose_now_Available_in_Canada_Central_and_Asia_Pacific_Seoul/","postDateTime":"2018-06-13T12:05:03Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now Available in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. We are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Data Firehose in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-stream-real-time-data-in-apache-parquet-or-orc-format-using-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/stream_real_time_data_in_apache_parquet_or_orc_format_using_firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe have added support for Apache Parquet and Apache ORC formats in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, so you can stream real-time data into Amazon S3 for cost-effective storage and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApache Parquet and Apache ORC are columnar data formats that allow you to store and query data more efficiently and cost-effectively. You can now configure your Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to automatically convert data into Parquet or ORC format before delivering to your S3 bucket. There is no coding required, and you can query S3 data much faster using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/athena/\"\u003eAmazon Athena\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/spectrum/\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Spectrum\u003c/a\u003e, allowing you to save storage and query costs.\u0026nbsp;Usage based charges apply for data format conversion in Kinesis Data Firehose. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. To get started with Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of regions where Kinesis Data Firehose is available, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/stream_real_time_data_in_apache_parquet_or_orc_format_using_firehose/","postDateTime":"2018-05-10T17:51:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream Real-Time Data in Apache Parquet or ORC Format Using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe have added support for Apache Parquet and Apache ORC formats in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, so you can stream real-time data into Amazon S3 for cost-effective storage and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-simple-storage-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-simple-storage-service","description":"general:products/amazon-simple-storage-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-athena","description":"general:products/amazon-athena","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-three-more-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-three-more-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:21:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/streaming-data/\"\u003estreaming data\u003c/a\u003e into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Data Firehose in the US West (N. California), Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) regions. With the addition of these three regions, Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in 9 regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home#/wizard/nameAndSource\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-three-more-regions/","postDateTime":"2018-01-16T11:24:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now Available in Three More Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/streaming-data.html\"\u003estreaming data\u003c/a\u003e into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-the-general-availability-of-splunk-as-a-destination","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-the-general-availability-of-splunk-as-a-destination/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:45:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools, now supports Splunk as a delivery destination. Splunk is an operational intelligence tool for analyzing machine-generated data in real-time. You can now use Kinesis Data Firehose to stream data to your Splunk cluster in real-time at any scale. This integration supports Splunk versions with HTTP Event Collector (HEC), including Splunk Enterprise and Splunk Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html#console-to-es\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e. Kinesis Data Firehose is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), EU (Frankfurt), and EU (Ireland) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Splunk, please see the Splunk \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.splunk.com/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-the-general-availability-of-splunk-as-a-destination/","postDateTime":"2017-12-05T10:23:57Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose announces the general availability of Splunk as a destination","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools, now supports Splunk as a delivery destination. Splunk is an operational intelligence tool for analyzing machine-generated data in real-time. You can now use Kinesis Data Firehose to stream data to your Splunk cluster in real-time at any scale. This integration supports Splunk versions with HTTP Event Collector (HEC), including Splunk Enterprise and Splunk Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-08-amazon-kinesis-firehose-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-eu-frankfurt-and-us-east-ohio-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-kinesis-firehose-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-eu-frankfurt-and-us-east-ohio-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:22:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:48:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/streaming-data/\"\u003estreaming data\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;into AWS. It can capture, transform,\u0026nbsp;and load streaming data into\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/\"\u003eAmazon Redshift\u003c/a\u003e, and\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/elasticsearch-service/\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you are already using today.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    We are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Firehose in the EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and US East (Ohio) regions. With the addition of these three regions, Kinesis Firehose is now available in 6 regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo). \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, create a delivery stream in the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home#/wizard/nameAndSource\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or explore the Kinesis Firehose\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-kinesis-firehose-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-eu-frankfurt-and-us-east-ohio-regions/","postDateTime":"2017-08-24T14:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose is now available in Asia Pacific (Tokyo), EU (Frankfurt), and US East (Ohio) regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/streaming-data.html\"\u003estreaming data\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;into AWS. It can capture, transform,\u0026nbsp;and load streaming data into\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3.html\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/redshift.html\"\u003eAmazon Redshift\u003c/a\u003e, and\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/elasticsearch-service.html\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you are already using today.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-08-amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-read-data-directly-from-amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-read-data-directly-from-amazon-kinesis-streams/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:48:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. Today we have added a built-in integration that allows you to send streaming data from Kinesis Streams to Kinesis Firehose by configuring your stream as a data source to Kinesis Firehose using the console or API. You can now create and configure a Firehose delivery stream to automatically read data from your Kinesis streams and then deliver the data to destinations. This makes it easy for you to persist data in your streams to data stores such as Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Elasticsearch Service.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Kinesis Firehose is available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions. To get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e or explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\"\u003eKinesis Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-read-data-directly-from-amazon-kinesis-streams/","postDateTime":"2017-08-18T11:15:46Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose can now read data directly from Amazon Kinesis Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. Today we have added a built-in integration that allows you to send streaming data from Kinesis Streams to Kinesis Firehose by configuring your stream as a data source to Kinesis Firehose using the console or API. You can now create and configure a Firehose delivery stream to automatically read data from your Kinesis streams and then deliver the data to destinations. This makes it easy for you to persist data in your streams to data stores such as Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Elasticsearch Service.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-07-announcing-the-new-amazon-kinesis-firehose-management-console","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/07/announcing-the-new-amazon-kinesis-firehose-management-console/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:47:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                 Amazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to prepare and load real-time streaming data into AWS. The Kinesis Firehose management console is the primary tool for creating and managing Kinesis Firehose delivery streams. Today we have launched the redesigned Kinesis Firehose management console to make it even easier to use.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new console shown in the screenshot below offers an intuitive wizard to quickly create delivery streams, graphics to easily understand the data flow for each destination (Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Elasticsearch Service), a simple way to include AWS Lambda functions for data transformation, and an overall improved interface.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Firehose is available in US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions. To get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home#/wizard/nameAndSource\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Kinesis Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/07/announcing-the-new-amazon-kinesis-firehose-management-console/","postDateTime":"2017-07-19T14:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing the new Amazon Kinesis Firehose management console","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                 Amazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to prepare and load real-time streaming data into AWS. The Kinesis Firehose management console is the primary tool for creating and managing Kinesis Firehose delivery streams. Today we have launched the redesigned Kinesis Firehose management console to make it even easier to use.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-06-cloudwatch-events-now-supports-amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/06/cloudwatch-events-now-supports-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:58:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  We are excited to announce that \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/events/WhatIsCloudWatchEvents.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Events\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/details/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e as a target. Amazon CloudWatch Events enables you to respond quickly to application availability issues or configuration changes that might impact performance or security by notifying you of AWS resource changes in near-real-time. You simply write rules to indicate which events are of interest to your application and what automated action to take when a rule matches an event. You can, for example, invoke AWS Lambda functions or notify an Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS) topic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, you can send the matching events to any Amazon Kinesis Firehose delivery stream enabling you near real-time analytics of event data with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you’re already using today. Amazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into AWS services such as Amazon Kinesis Analytics, Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Elasticsearch etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have also published a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/big-data/visualize-and-monitor-amazon-ec2-events-with-amazon-cloudwatch-events-and-amazon-kinesis-firehose/\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e on how you can use this new feature to monitor and get near real time analytics on EC2 events.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease visit the following pages for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/events/WhatIsCloudWatchEvents.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Events\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eRegional Availability\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/06/cloudwatch-events-now-supports-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","postDateTime":"2017-06-16T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon CloudWatch Events now supports Amazon Kinesis Firehose as a target","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  We are excited to announce that \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/events/WhatIsCloudWatchEvents.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Events\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose/details.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e as a target. Amazon CloudWatch Events enables you to respond quickly to application availability issues or configuration changes that might impact performance or security by notifying you of AWS resource changes in near-real-time. You simply write rules to indicate which events are of interest to your application and what automated action to take when a rule matches an event. You can, for example, invoke AWS Lambda functions or notify an Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS) topic.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-04-amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-price-reduction-and-tiered-pricing-plan","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/04/amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-price-reduction-and-tiered-pricing-plan/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:52:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                 We are excited to announce a 17% price reduction for Amazon Kinesis Firehose from $0.035 per GB to $0.029 per GB of data ingested. We have also introduced a tiered pricing plan to further reduce prices by an additional 26% to as low as $0.020 per GB of data ingested when your data volume reaches certain tier. With these two changes, you can now save up to 43% in costs when loading streaming data using Amazon Kinesis Firehose. For more information, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                 \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to prepare and load real-time streaming data into AWS. To get started, see the Amazon Kinesis Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html#console-to-es\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e and our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/getting-started/\"\u003egetting started page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:23Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/04/amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-price-reduction-and-tiered-pricing-plan/","postDateTime":"2017-04-06T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose announces price reduction and tiered pricing plan","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                 We are excited to announce a 17% price reduction for Amazon Kinesis Firehose from $0.035 per GB to $0.029 per GB of data ingested. We have also introduced a tiered pricing plan to further reduce prices by an additional 26% to as low as $0.020 per GB of data ingested when your data volume reaches certain tier. With these two changes, you can now save up to 43% in costs when loading streaming data using Amazon Kinesis Firehose. For more information, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose/pricing.html\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:06:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e to prepare your streaming data before it is loaded to data stores. With this new feature, you can easily convert raw streaming data from your data sources into formats required by your destination data stores, without having to build your own data processing pipelines.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use this feature, simply select an AWS Lambda function from the Amazon Kinesis Firehose delivery stream configuration tab in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Kinesis Firehose will automatically apply that function to every input data record and load the transformed data to destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose provides pre-built Lambda blueprints for converting common data sources such as Apache logs and system logs to JSON and CSV formats. You can use these pre-built blueprints without any change, or customize them further, or write your own custom functions. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Firehose to automatically retry failed jobs and back up the raw streaming data.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about this feature, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eData Transformation\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Firehose developer guide.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Kinesis Analytics, and Amazon S3. To get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, sign into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Firehose, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores/","postDateTime":"2016-12-21T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose can now prepare and transform streaming data before loading it to data stores","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e to prepare your streaming data before it is loaded to data stores. With this new feature, you can easily convert raw streaming data from your data sources into formats required by your destination data stores, without having to build your own data processing pipelines.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-11-test-drive-amazon-kinesis-firehose-using-built-in-sample-data","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/test-drive-amazon-kinesis-firehose-using-built-in-sample-data/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:02:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the ability to test drive \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e using built-in sample data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into Amazon Kinesis Analytics, Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Elasticsearch Service, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards. With a click of a button in the console, you can now ingest simulated stock price data and use it to test your Firehose delivery stream configuration. The simulated stock price data is generated automatically and sent continuously to your delivery stream. This allows you to test your delivery stream setup without having to write code to generate your own test data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollowing is a console screenshot of this new feature:\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStandard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/pricing/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose charges\u003c/a\u003e apply when your delivery stream is transmitting the sample data, but there is no charge associated with the generation of the data. You can stop the sample stream at any time from the console and stop incurring usage charges.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003esign into the console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-10-11T22:14:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/test-drive-amazon-kinesis-firehose-using-built-in-sample-data/","postDateTime":"2016-11-07T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Test drive Amazon Kinesis Firehose using built-in sample data","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the ability to test drive \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e using built-in sample data.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-08-introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/08/introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:32:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed service for continuously querying streaming data using standard SQL. With Kinesis Analytics, you can write standard SQL queries on streaming data and gain actionable insights in real-time, without having to learn any new programming skills.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can get started with Kinesis Analytics in minutes with three easy steps in the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. First, you select a Kinesis stream or Kinesis Firehose delivery stream as the input stream. Kinesis Analytics ingests the data, automatically recognizes standard data formats including JSON, CSV, and TSV, and suggests a schema. You can refine this schema, or if your data is unstructured, you can define a new one using our intuitive schema editor. Next, you use the Kinesis Analytics SQL editor and pre-built templates to write your SQL queries. Lastly, you point to where you want Kinesis Analytics to load processed results. Kinesis Analytics takes care of everything required to continuously run your queries, and automatically scales to match the volume and throughput rate of incoming data while delivering sub-second processing latencies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Analytics is closely integrated with other AWS services so you can build complete stream processing solutions using services you are already familiar with. It integrates out-of-box with Kinesis Streams and Kinesis Firehose so it’s easy to ingest streaming data and send processed results to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, or your own custom destination.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Kinesis Analytics, you only pay for the resources your queries use. There is no minimum fee or setup cost. For more information on Kinesis Analytics pricing, see the pricing page.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics is currently available in the following AWS Regions: N. Virginia, Oregon, and Ireland. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Analytics, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/analytics/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e, this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-kinesis-analytics-process-streaming-data-in-real-time-with-sql\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/kinesis/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with Kinesis Analytics, visit the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/08/introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics/","postDateTime":"2016-08-11T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Kinesis Analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed service for continuously querying streaming data using standard SQL. With Kinesis Analytics, you can write standard SQL queries on streaming data and gain actionable insights in real-time, without having to learn any new programming skills.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":69,"totalHits":69},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}